    "stopped": "Stopped after the first two SanDisk runs: the user reported the drive overheating, after about 40 minutes in which it served ~0.5 TB of reads at up to 1 GB/s (the copy, cache flushes, and each run's load reading the whole 63 GB file). Their 1.0 tok/s, against 10.7 in decode_gpt_oss_120b, is taken as thermal throttling: not a measurement of speculation. Internal-SSD runs not done.",
    "finding": "Internal SSD: 2.0 tok/s with and without drafts (prompt included). Prompt lookup drafted 14 tokens and 7 were accepted in 108: the type-hinted answer rarely repeats the original's token runs, so this prompt cannot show whether speculation pays more when the drive is the limit."
  },
