  "real_text_readahead_vs_mmap": {
    "note": "scratchpad realtext.py / realtext.sh, internal SSD only: gpt-oss-120b real greedy decoding, 64 tokens after each of 28 different prompts (4 per process, no prompt reused, so no process inherits another's experts), processes in the order mmap(count-only), readahead, readahead, mmap(count-only), plain, readahead, plain. plain = mmap with nothing else; mmap = mmap with read-ahead only counting missing bytes (mincore), which itself cost ~2.6 s per 64 tokens; readahead = Turing's read-ahead, defaults (adaptive, 16 threads, blocking). Generations that hit end-of-text early are shorter than 64 tokens.",
